<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI40-WINDOWS-SQLITE-CONNECTION-LEAK>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI40-WINDOWS-SQLITE-CONNECTION-LEAK" ;
  triage:title "verify_durable_admissions leaves the read-only SQLite connection open, breaking Windows tempdir cleanup and CI on both AI.40 and AI.43" ;
  triage:description "scripts/smoke/run_admission_capacity.py:672 uses `with sqlite3.connect(uri, uri=True) as connection:` to read the durability count. Python's sqlite3.Connection context manager only commits/rolls back the transaction on exit -- it does NOT close the connection or release the underlying file handle. On Windows this leaves the mail.db file locked, so the enclosing tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() cleanup in the test fails with PermissionError: [WinError 32] The process cannot access the file because it is being used by another process. Confirmed live and reproducing on both PR #708 (feature/pAI-s40-local-transport-benchmark, the source of this code) and PR #710 (feature/pAI-s43-remote-https-response-framing, which inherited it via merge-forward) -- both show 'Just lint (windows-latest)' and 'Test (windows-latest)' CI failures with the identical traceback (test_durability_verification_counts_every_isolated_sqlite_row_after_restart, tempfile.py cleanup -> PermissionError on mail.db). This is a real, reproducible Windows-only regression, not CI infra flake. Fix: explicitly call connection.close() (or wrap with contextlib.closing(sqlite3.connect(...))) so the file handle is released before the test's TemporaryDirectory exits." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "windows-portability" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-08-01T07:20:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AI40 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-08-01T07:15:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI40-WINDOWS-SQLITE-CONNECTION-LEAK/S40-1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI40-WINDOWS-SQLITE-CONNECTION-LEAK/S43-1> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "1" .

<urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI40-WINDOWS-SQLITE-CONNECTION-LEAK/S40-1>
  a triage:Occurrence ;
  triage:file "scripts/smoke/run_admission_capacity.py" ;
  triage:line 699 ;
  triage:snippet "FIXED at c73ab129 (AI40-QA-5). test_run_admission_capacity.py's fixture connections (now lines 294 and 309) both use `with closing(__import__(\"sqlite3\").connect(database)) as connection:`; verify_durable_admissions (run_admission_capacity.py:699) already used closing(). New dedicated regression test test_durability_verification_closes_the_read_only_sqlite_connection (lines 319-339) mocks sqlite3.connect and asserts .closed is True. Confirmed independently by quality-mgr direct read, and corroborated in full by both arch-qa and req-qa during AI40-QA-5. gh pr checks 708 on c73ab129 (run 30692034345) shows all 8 legs green, including Just lint (windows-latest) and Test (windows-latest). Genuinely fixed; closing this occurrence. NOTE: the S43-1 occurrence (feature/pAI-s43-remote-https-response-framing) remains a SEPARATE, still-open occurrence -- this fix has not been merge-forwarded onto that branch (confirmed AI43-QA-3) -- so the Finding stays open overall." ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:closed true ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-08-01T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:branch "feature/pAI-s40-local-transport-benchmark" ;
  triage:headSha "c73ab129" ;
  triage:occursIn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/S40/c73ab129> .

<urn:atm:triage:occurrence/AI40-WINDOWS-SQLITE-CONNECTION-LEAK/S43-1>
  a triage:Occurrence ;
  triage:file "scripts/smoke/run_admission_capacity.py" ;
  triage:line 672 ;
  triage:snippet "FIXED at 307d39a8 (AI43-QA-4). The AI40 fix genuinely merge-forwarded: verify_durable_admissions (run_admission_capacity.py:699) uses `with closing(sqlite3.connect(uri, uri=True)) as connection:`; test_run_admission_capacity.py's fixture connections (lines 294, 309) both use `with closing(__import__(\"sqlite3\").connect(database)) as connection:`. Confirmed independently by quality-mgr direct grep of both files at 307d39a8, corroborated by arch-qa and req-qa during AI43-QA-4. `gh pr checks 710` at 307d39a8 (run 30693290506): all 8 legs green including Just lint (windows-latest) and Test (windows-latest). `git merge-base --is-ancestor c73ab129 HEAD` independently confirmed true by quality-mgr in the AI.43 worktree. Both S40-1 and S43-1 occurrences are now fixed; Finding closes overall." ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:closed true ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-08-01T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:branch "feature/pAI-s43-remote-https-response-framing" ;
  triage:headSha "307d39a8" ;
  triage:occursIn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/S43/362801f6> .

